<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" updated="August 20, 2026">
  <p>This site, gregtoler.com, is run by Greg Toler, operating as GT Strategies ("I", "me").
  This page explains what information the site collects, why, and what happens to it.
  The short version: I collect what you choose to send me through the contact form so I
  can reply, and I don't sell or share it for marketing.</p>

  <h2>What I collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>What you type into the contact form</strong> — your situation, the areas it
    touches, your message, your name, work email, and optionally a phone number, LinkedIn
    URL, and preferred way to be contacted.</li>
    <li><strong>Basic technical data</strong> that any web server receives — IP address,
    browser type, pages requested — held briefly in hosting logs by Cloudflare, which
    serves this site.</li>
    <li><strong>A small browser preference</strong> (theme / accent) stored locally on your
    device. It never leaves your browser and is not a tracking cookie.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I do not run advertising trackers or sell data. <span class="note">[CONFIRM] If analytics
  (e.g. Google Analytics) is added to this version of the site, list it here and in the
  cookie section.</span></p>

  <h2>How I use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To read and reply to your inquiry. Form submissions are delivered to me as a
    message in my private Slack workspace.</li>
    <li>To sort genuine inquiries from spam. Submissions are run through an automated
    screening step powered by OpenAI's API, which returns a yes/no on whether the message
    looks like a real request for my services. OpenAI processes the text for that purpose
    under its API terms and, per its policy, does not use API data to train its models. If
    the screen passes, the site offers you a calendar to book a call.</li>
    <li>To schedule a call if you choose to. The booking calendar is Google Calendar's
    appointment scheduling, embedded on this site. Anything you enter there goes to Google
    and is governed by <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>Only the services needed to run the site and reply to you: Cloudflare (hosting),
  Slack (where your inquiry lands), OpenAI (the spam screen), and Google (calendar
  booking, if you use it). None of them are given your information for their own
  marketing. I don't sell personal information.</p>

  <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
  <p>Inquiries stay in my Slack and email until I delete them, which I do periodically
  for inquiries that didn't lead to a conversation. If we work together, your details
  become part of that engagement's records. <span class="note">[CONFIRM] retention habit —
  adjust if you keep or purge on a schedule.</span></p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:greg@gregtoler.com">greg@gregtoler.com</a> to ask what I hold
  about you, to correct it, or to have it deleted. I'll do that unless I'm required to
  keep it. You can also simply not use the form — LinkedIn works too.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>This site doesn't set tracking cookies. The embedded Google Calendar booking widget
  may set Google cookies when it loads. Your browser's theme preference is stored in
  local storage, not a cookie.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is for businesses and working professionals and isn't directed at anyone
  under 18.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top will change with it.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Greg Toler, GT Strategies &middot; <a href="mailto:greg@gregtoler.com">greg@gregtoler.com</a>
  <span class="note">[CONFIRM] add a mailing address / state if you want one listed — some
  jurisdictions expect it.</span></p>
</LegalPage>
